+Cracks and Crevices 0.5 (build 757) provenance
+==============================================
+
+Upstream game source
+--------------------
+Original URL: https://redmine.bloodycactus.com/attachments/download/32/cracks_and_crevices-0.5.tar.bz2
+Retrieved URL (Wayback snapshot): https://web.archive.org/web/20150804175538if_/https://redmine.bloodycactus.com/attachments/download/32/cracks_and_crevices-0.5.tar.bz2
+Size: 121192 bytes
+MD5: dd6e27a5bfea81549c94d52c12b9682e
+SHA256: a00cf6ab0a189673fe152f9325b14c1a6b6a531a8510d1cc321c44ccdeb9fb66
+Version: 0.5 (source VersionString v0.05/0757; version.c:12-29, docs/readme.txt:1, Makefile:2)
+
+Recovered libfov archive (fov.c/fov.h reference Greg McIntyre COPYING, omitted
+from the game tarball)
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+URL: https://storage.googleapis.com/google-code-archive-source/v2/code.google.com/libfov/source-archive.zip
+SHA256: 7dfc0ff6b53ef6002e5ff072807e1f26e72f39a5bef2ef9ed6ee7651881d3586
+License member: libfov/trunk/COPYING
+Member SHA256: 52aff126c6c7d33284e2e8fb9ff29e05eb03aff8ded0cd7f0914086b6fb513ca
+The COPYING member is MIT (copyright (c) 2006 Greg McIntyre); the libfov
+ChangeLog dates the license change from BSD to MIT at 2007-09-03. The full
+text is shipped as COPYING.libfov in source and licenses/COPYING.libfov when installed.
+
+Nature of source used
+---------------------
+The vendored libfov sources carry the same copyright, API, and algorithm as the
+recovered upstream libfov archive but include local edits; they are NOT
+byte-identical to upstream. The game itself is derived from the released
+cracks_and_crevices-0.5 source described above.
+
+License coverage
+----------------
+- The project as a whole: docs/readme.txt:4-5 releases the project under the
+  GNU General Public License version 2; docs/COPYING supplies the GPL2 text.
+  This is a GPLv2 grant, not an explicit "or later" grant.
+- MT19937 (random_mt.c:10-38): BSD 3-clause redistribution grant by Makoto
+  Matsumoto and Takuji Nishimura, 1997-2002. When installed, the entire
+  original notice must be reproduced separately; the project GPL2 COPYING is
+  not that grant.
+- MEMWATCH (memwatch.c:3-26, memwatch.h): GPL 2 or later, Johan Lindh. The
+  bundled release object does not activate MEMWATCH; its notice is retained
+  with the source.
+- Fonts (font_8x16.inc, font_12x16.inc, font_14x24.inc, embedded PCX
+  payloads): no per-file provenance or license notice exists in the project.
+  Distribution is retained under the project-wide GPLv2 statement, which
+  supports distribution of the author's project contents without proving
+  outside origin. No claim of author-drawn origin is made here.
+- libfov: separate MIT notice, see above.
+
+Runtime state layout
+--------------------
+The game resolves its state directory at runtime: it uses the absolute
+XDG_STATE_HOME value when set, otherwise falls back to $HOME/.local/state.
+Within that state directory the "cracks-and-crevices" subdirectory holds the
+game's config, save.bin, scores, and chardump.txt files. HOME itself is never
+modified. Scores are kept per-user in the state directory; the game does not
+use a shared /var/games location.
